This one required a bit of research. However, our first result - https://www.huntress.com/cybersecurity-101/topic/what-is-false-flag-in-cybersecurity - tells us the answer is: false flag.

True or false: a defender's primary job during an active incident is to determine which nation-state is responsible.
As we just read - Your job in most security roles is not to name the attacker. It is to understand what they were after, stop the bleeding, and build defenses that hold regardless of who sent the attack.
